---
import { site } from '../config/site';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';

const url = `${site.url}/contact/`;

const schema = [
  {
    '@type': 'ContactPage',
    '@id': `${url}#page`,
    name: `Contact ${site.name}`,
    url,
    isPartOf: { '@id': `${site.url}/#website` },
    about: { '@id': `${site.url}/#organization` },
  },
  {
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    '@id': `${url}#breadcrumbs`,
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: `${site.url}/` },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Contact', item: url },
    ],
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Contact Us | ${site.name}`}
  description="Call (773) 302-2292 to reach a local roofer for roof leak repair in Severna Park, MD, or email us about the site. No forms, no obligation."
  schema={schema}
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Contact"
    title="Call about your roof leak"
    lede="The fastest way to get help is a phone call. Tell us where the water is showing up and you'll be connected with a local roofing provider."
    crumb="Contact"
  />

  <section class="section section--white">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="contact-grid">
        <article class="card" data-reveal>
          <span class="icon-tile icon-tile--accent"><Icon name="phone" /></span>
          <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem">Phone</h2>
          <a class="contact-card" href={site.phone.href} data-call><strong>{site.phone.display}</strong></a>
          <p>For leaks, storm damage and repair questions. Calls are connected to a local provider.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card" data-reveal>
          <span class="icon-tile"><Icon name="mail" /></span>
          <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem">Email</h2>
          <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}><strong>{site.email}</strong></a>
          <p>For questions about this website, corrections or feedback. Not for urgent leaks.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card" data-reveal>
          <span class="icon-tile"><Icon name="pin" /></span>
          <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem">Service area</h2>
          <p><strong>{site.city}, {site.state} {site.zip}</strong></p>
          <p>Plus Arnold, Pasadena, Millersville, Severn and Glen Burnie. There's no walk-in office.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--off">
    <div class="container container--narrow prose" data-content>
      <h2>What happens when you call?</h2>
      <p>
        You'll describe the leak: where water appears inside, when it started and what the weather was. Your call is
        then connected to an independent roofing provider who serves {site.city}. They'll ask a few more questions,
        talk about timing and arrange to look at the roof. Calling is free and you're under no obligation to book
        anything.
      </p>
      <p>
        If water is coming in right now, say so at the start of the call. While you wait, follow the first steps on the
        <a href="/emergency-roof-leak-repair/">emergency roof leak repair</a> page: catch the water, switch off power to
        any wet fixture and stay off the roof.
      </p>
      <h2>Why is there no contact form?</h2>
      <p>
        A leaking roof is easier to explain by phone, and a provider can ask the right follow-up questions straight away.
        We've kept the site to calls only so nothing gets lost in an inbox. If you'd like to understand the likely cause
        before you call, the <a href="/#checker">symptom checker on the homepage</a> is a good place to start, and
        <a href="/roof-leak-detection/">roof leak detection</a> explains how hidden leaks are traced.
      </p>
      <h2>When should you email instead?</h2>
      <p>
        Email is best for anything that isn't an active leak: a correction to one of the guides, a question about how
        the referral works, a privacy request, or feedback about a provider you were connected with. We aim to read
        every email, but we're not a dispatch desk, so please always phone for a leak.
      </p>
      <aside class="callout callout--tip"><p><strong>Pro tip:</strong> Take two or three photos before you call: the stain inside, the area of roof above it from the ground, and anything in the yard after a storm. They help the provider plan the visit.</p></aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
